title: <span style="color: var(--dvp-color);">**[+ dvp_name +]**</span> Party Congress
view-if: lvp_formed and year == lvp_next_congress_year and month == lvp_next_congress_month
on-arrival: lvp_next_congress_year = year + 2
tags: event
new-page: true

= <span style="color: var(--dvp-color);">**[+ dvp_name +]**</span> Party Congress

The German liberal movement has been notoriously factionalised since the days of the Empire. However, the scarring rise of the Nazis has pushed our parties into action. The left-liberal <span style="color: #DCCA4A;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>, Right-Liberal <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>, and some special interest groups have finally united together into the <span style="color: var(--dvp-color);">**Liberal People’s Party**</span>. Several leadership candidates have emerged for this & upcoming conferences, with three main blocs of support; Labour and the Progressive factions of the <span style="color: var(--dvp-color);">**[+ dvp_name +]**</span> have coalesced into a ‘social republican bloc’, the centres of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> and <span style="color: #DCCA4A;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> have merged into a ‘pragmatic centre’ bloc, and, of course, the industrialists remain on the fringes.

- @congress: The party will elect its leader for the next 2 years.

@congress
on-arrival: {!
Q.total_influence = 0;
Q.progressive_influence = 0;
Q.democratic_influence = 0;
Q.liberal_influence = 0;
Q.labor_influence = 0;
Q.industrialist_influence = 0;
Q.special_interest_influence = 0;

Q.dbp_influence = 0;
Q.wp_influence = 0;



if (Q.progressives_dvp) {
    Q.total_influence = parseFloat((Q.total_influence + Q.progressive_strength).toFixed(1))
}
if (Q.democrats_dvp) {
    Q.total_influence = parseFloat((Q.total_influence + Q.democratic_strength).toFixed(1))
}
if (Q.liberals_dvp) {
    Q.total_influence = parseFloat((Q.total_influence + Q.liberal_strength).toFixed(1))
}
if (Q.labor_dvp) {
    Q.total_influence = parseFloat((Q.total_influence + Q.labor_strength).toFixed(1))
}
if (Q.industrialists_dvp) {
    Q.total_influence = parseFloat((Q.total_influence + Q.industrialist_strength).toFixed(1))
}

if (Q.special_interest_dvp) {
    Q.total_influence = parseFloat((Q.total_influence + Q.special_interest_strength).toFixed(1))
    Q.total_special_interest = 0;
    if (Q.dbp_dvp) {
        Q.dbp_share = parseFloat((Q.rural_dvp*(Q.progressive_strength + Q.democratic_strength + Q.liberal_strength)*0.05).toFixed(1))
        Q.total_special_interest += Q.dbp_share
    }
    if (Q.wp_dvp) {
        Q.wp_share = parseFloat((Q.new_middle_dvp + Q.old_middle_dvp).toFixed(1))
        Q.total_special_interest += Q.wp_share
    }
}



if (Q.progressives_dvp) Q.progressive_influence = parseFloat((Q.progressive_strength/Q.total_influence*100).toFixed(1))
if (Q.democrats_dvp) Q.democratic_influence = parseFloat((Q.democratic_strength/Q.total_influence*100).toFixed(1))
if (Q.liberals_dvp) Q.liberal_influence = parseFloat((Q.liberal_strength/Q.total_influence*100).toFixed(1))
if (Q.labor_dvp) Q.labor_influence = parseFloat((Q.labor_strength/Q.total_influence*100).toFixed(1))
if (Q.industrialists_dvp) Q.industrialist_influence = parseFloat((Q.industrialist_strength/Q.total_influence*100).toFixed(1))

if (Q.dbp_dvp) Q.dbp_influence = parseFloat((Q.special_interest_strength*(Q.dbp_share/Q.total_special_interest)/Q.total_influence*100).toFixed(1))
if (Q.wp_dvp) Q.wp_influence = parseFloat((Q.special_interest_strength*(Q.wp_share/Q.total_special_interest)/Q.total_influence*100).toFixed(1))
!}
on-display: {!
data = []
if (Q.progressives_dvp) {
    data.push({
        "id": "rdp",
        "legend": "Progressives",
        "name": "Progressives",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.progressive_influence*5.0),
    });
}
if (Q.democrats_dvp) {
    data.push({
        "id": "ddp",
        "legend": "Democrats",
        "name": "Democrats",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.democratic_influence*5.0),
    });
}
if (Q.dbp_dvp) {
    data.push({
        "id": "dbp",
        "legend": "Farmer Groups",
        "name": "Farmer Groups",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.dbp_influence*5.0),
    });
}
if (Q.labor_dvp) {
    data.push({
        "id": "labor",
        "legend": "Labor",
        "name": "Labor",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.labor_influence*5.0),
    });
}
if (Q.liberals_dvp) {
    data.push({
        "id": "nlp",
        "legend": "Liberals",
        "name": "Liberals",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.liberal_influence*5.0),
    });
}
if (Q.wp_dvp) {
    data.push({
        "id": "wp",
        "legend": "Middle Class Groups",
        "name": "Middle Class Groups",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.wp_influence*5.0),
    });
}
if (Q.industrialists_dvp) {
    data.push({
        "id": "dvp_2",
        "legend": "Industrialists",
        "name": "Industrialists",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.industrialist_influence*5.0),
    });
}

if (window && d3) {
    var width = 500; 
    var height = 500;
    var screenWidth = document.getElementById('content').offsetWidth;
    if (screenWidth < width - 50) {
        width = screenWidth - 50; 
        height = width;
        document.getElementById("reichstag").style.height = screenWidth/2 + "px";
    } 

    var parliament = d3.parliament();
    parliament.width(width).height(height).innerRadiusCoef(0.4);
    parliament.enter.fromCenter(true).smallToBig(true);
    parliament.exit.toCenter(false).bigToSmall(true);
    d3.select("#reichstag").datum(data).call(parliament);
}
!}
go-to: leader

= <span style="color: var(--dvp-color);">**[+ dvp_name +]**</span> Party Congress

{!<svg id="reichstag" style="width: 500px; height: 250px;"> </svg>!}

{!<table>!}
{!<tr><td>Organization</td><td>Delegates Share</td>!}
[? if progressives_dvp: {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#E0B0FF'> </div> !} Progressives: {!</td><td>!} [+ progressive_influence +]% {!</td><td>!} ?]

[? if democrats_dvp: {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#DCCA4A'> </div> !} Democrats: {!</td><td>!} [+ democratic_influence +]% {!</td><td>!} ?]

[? if dbp_dvp: {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#38C538'> </div> !} Farmer Groups: {!</td><td>!} [+ dbp_influence +]% {!</td><td>!} ?]

[? if labor_dvp: {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#6D5298'> </div> !} Labor: {!</td><td>!} [+ labor_influence +]% {!</td><td>!} ?]

[? if liberals_dvp: {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#98C22C'> </div> !} Liberals: {!</td><td>!} [+ liberal_influence +]% {!</td><td>!} ?]

[? if wp_dvp: {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#B8996F'> </div> !} Middle Class Groups: {!</td><td>!} [+ wp_influence +]% {!</td><td>!} ?]

[? if industrialists_dvp: {!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#C0A054'> </div> !} Industrialists: {!</td><td>!} [+ industrialist_influence +]% {!</td><td>!} ?]
{!</table>!}

@leader
on-arrival: {!
!}

WIP

- @lemmer: Ernst Lemmer will lead our party.
- @luther: Hans Luther will lead our party.
- @curtius: Julius Curtius will lead our party.
- @heuss: Theodor Heuss will lead our party.

@lemmer
subtitle: Lemmer is a prominent labor leader. <span style="color: #E0B0FF;">**Progressives**</span> + <span style="color: #DCCA4A;">**Democrats**</span> + <span style="color: #6D5298;">**Labor**</span> ([+ progressive_influence + democratic_influence + labor_influence +]%)
unavailable-subtitle: Lemmer isn’t seen as a viable candidate, with the party viewing him as too left-wing. He has endorsed Dietrich or Thiel. <span style="color: #E0B0FF;">**Progressives**</span> + <span style="color: #DCCA4A;">**Democrats**</span> + <span style="color: #6D5298;">**Labor**</span> ([+ progressive_influence + democratic_influence + labor_influence +]%)
choose-if: progressive_influence + democratic_influence + labor_influence >= 50
on-arrival: dvp_leader = "Lemmer"; progressive_strength += 10; democratization += 1; progressive_dissent -= 5; spd_relation += 5
face-image: img/portraits/LemmerErnst.jpg

Ernst Lemmer has managed to, with the backing of Thiel’s unions, and the former <span style="color: #DCCA4A;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>, become leader of the <span style="color: var(--dvp-color);">**[+ dvp_name +]**</span>. He is expected to cooperate closely with Thiel, and the socialists of the <span style="color: #E3000F;">**SPD**</span> will be watching his leadership closely. He will certainly be a divisive leader of the <span style="color: var(--dvp-color);">**[+ dvp_name +]**</span>, with his progressive stance sure to render any cooperation with the parties to our right difficult for the near future.
  

@heuss
subtitle: Heuss was a former member of the <span style="color: #DCCA4A;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>'s business wing. <span style="color: #E0B0FF;">**Progressives**</span> + <span style="color: #DCCA4A;">**Democrats**</span> + <span style="color: #98C22C;">**Liberals**</span> ([+ progressive_influence + democratic_influence + liberal_influence +]%)
unavailable-subtitle: The party prefers a former <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> member than Heuss, with the <span style="color: #DCCA4A;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> not holding enough sway. Heuss has endorsed Curtius. <span style="color: #E0B0FF;">**Progressives**</span> + <span style="color: #DCCA4A;">**Democrats**</span> + <span style="color: #98C22C;">**Liberals**</span> ([+ progressive_influence + democratic_influence + liberal_influence +]%)
choose-if: progressive_influence + democratic_influence + liberal_influence >= 50
on-arrival: dvp_leader = "Heuss"; democratic_strength += 10; democratization += 1; democratic_dissent -= 5; z_relation += 5; kvp_relation += 3
face-image: img/portraits/HeussTheodor.jpg

Heuss Dietrich has been elected as the leader of the <span style="color: var(--dvp-color);">**[+ dvp_name +]**</span>. Having a former <span style="color: #DCCA4A;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> member at the helm of the party will shift it leftwards, especially due to his genuine, determined commitment to liberal democracy.
  

@luther
subtitle: The former Chancellor is always available as a compromise candidate.
unavailable-subtitle: Luther sees no need to run, currently.
#choose-if: 
on-arrival: dvp_leader = "Luther"
face-image: img/portraits/LutherHans.jpg

Hans Luther, [? if not president = "Luther": president of the Reichsbank?][? if president = "Luther": President of the Republic?], has been elected, commanding great confidence amongst the party’s many factions. He is, however, as the [? if not president = "Luther": president of the Reichsbank?][? if president = "Luther": President of the Republic?], expected to take a hands-off approach, delegating the party’s day to day running to his former <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> allies Curtius and Thiel. All in all, many view him as simply a caretaker until their faction can seize power at the next congress. We shall see how accurate they are.
  

@curtius
subtitle: Curtius belongs to the Stresemannite wing of our party. <span style="color: #98C22C;">**Liberals**</span> + <span style="color: #6D5298;">**Labor**</span> [? if peoples_conservatives_dvp: + <span style="color: #0087DC;">**People's Conservatives**</span> ?] ([+ liberal_influence + labor_influence + peoples_conservative_influence +]%)
unavailable-subtitle: Curtius prefers Thiel or Dietrich currently, with the former <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> too weak to push him, anyways. <span style="color: #98C22C;">**Liberals**</span> + <span style="color: #6D5298;">**Labor**</span> [? if peoples_conservatives_dvp: + <span style="color: #0087DC;">**People's Conservatives**</span> ?] ([+ liberal_influence + labor_influence + peoples_conservative_influence +]%)
choose-if: liberal_influence + labor_influence + peoples_conservative_influence >= 50
on-arrival: dvp_leader = "Curtius"; liberal_strength += 10; democratization += 1; liberal_dissent -= 5;
face-image: img/portraits/CurtiusJulius.jpg

Julius Curtius, Stresemann’s successor, has been elected as the leader of the <span style="color: var(--dvp-color);">**[+ dvp_name +]**</span>. Whilst he may alienate the extremes of the party, his foreign policy experience and the mantle of Stresemann’s successor will help him be a strong <span style="color: var(--dvp-color);">**[+ dvp_name +]**</span> leader. He is expected to be a similar leader to Stresemann, furthering his ‘party of reason’ ideals.
